'' TKO0930, fbc's 73 (T22): a whole array as an assignment target or a 'swap' operand --
'' from another array of either size, a dynamic one, a string array, a field array, the
'' 'a( ) = b( )' spelling (fbc's 181 there), '+=', a scalar, and 'swap a, c'. tiko
'' accepted them and copied the source's byte size into the destination, overrunning a
'' smaller one, or dropped a 'swap' of two sizes in silence. Accepted, as by fbc: a record
'' assignment, an element, a fixed-length string, and swapping two elements -- and tiko's
'' own extension, 'd = MakeArr( )' moving an array result into a dynamic array. Lines
'' identical to fbc-modern's errors. See WholeArray_ in symbols/arrresult.bas.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --dump-ir tests/diagnostics/src/array-whole-assign.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 1
